{"id": "EUVD-2026-102281", "enisaUuid": "6e354c74-cf21-359f-b3c0-f449a5fe4b53", "description": "libTiMidity through 0.2.8 contains a stack out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the SoundFont loader that allows attackers to corrupt stack memory via unchecked generator operators in parse_gen. Attackers can supply a crafted .sf2 file with out-of-range pgen/igen operator values to write chosen 16-bit values near the stack Layer object, causing crashes and stack memory corruption.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:42", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libtimidity-soundfont-generator-oper-oob-write", "https://github.com/sezero/libtimidity/blob/a52adf6aee2635e2a16797213a089c2180e67757/src/sndfont.c#L468-L480", "https://github.com/sezero/libtimidity", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtimidity-through-0.2.8-stack-out-of-bounds-write-via-parse-gen-in-soundfont-loader"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111154", "GHSA-qg69-jphp-p9g8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b7ff3f51-ca5e-369b-845b-edfcdf4ecf2d", "product": {"name": "libtimidity", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}, "product_version": "0.2.8 \u22640.2.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91f24b2f-25ac-3204-b15f-d5b29a79e2e3", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}], "isExploited": false}